From f1f9a9b5e713c7323ef8f74c4d60d07af5587cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:28:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] blockstorage: back BlockManager::m_block_index (BlockMap)
 with ChunkedSlabAllocator

Every CBlockIndex in BlockMap was a separate ::operator new allocation,
scattering headers across the heap and costing cache/TLB misses on
pprev and GetAncestor() walks (median time past, ASERT anchors,
locators).

Back BlockMap with ChunkedSlabAllocator so nodes are carved from
16384-slot contiguous chunks and recycled through an intrusive
freelist. Slots never move, preserving the stable CBlockIndex
addressing validation depends on. Bucket arrays (n > 1) still use
aligned operator new. All mutation already happens under cs_main.

src/support/allocators/chunked_slab.h is byte-identical to the header
added by ecash patch 043 (sha256 da1beaad...2c887d) so the two series
share one ChunkedSlabAllocator definition.

Add a test that forces several rehashes and checks pointer stability,
chunk count and slot reuse after erase.
